{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the blood of the grape you drank, wine.</b> He called the beverage that comes from grapes 'blood' because it is red like it. And furthermore, in the secret of the language, it is called 'blood' on account of the fact that it caused death and brought blood into the world — this according to the opinion of the one who says 'he squeezed grapes and brought it to him.' And the term ענב is the single berry; this indicates the extraordinary abundance and overflow of blessing in the land, for from a single berry much drink came forth. Now it is known that the berries are called ענבים, and the cluster upon which they hang is collectively called אשכול in the language of the Torah, and in the language of the Rabbis, פרכיל. And so they said in the first chapter of Sukkah: 'a פרכיל of grapes, and within it grapes,' for thus the grapes suspended on the vine are called אשכולות, and that upon which the clusters hang is called גפן if attached, and זמורה if detached — and this is (Numbers 13:23): ״ויכרתו משם זמורה ואשכול ענבים אחד״ — and the verse testifies to the abundance of the land's blessing and to the greatness of its fruit, for upon that severed זמורה there was only אשכול ענבים אחד — a single cluster of grapes — and therefore it adds אחד, for each one took a single separate item: one a cluster, one a pomegranate, one a fig."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:13.576673702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}